  "body": "how come that this logs two matches\r\n```js\r\np = 'http://a/b/*'\r\nconsole.log(new URLPattern(p).exec('http://a/b/')?.pathname.groups)\r\nconsole.log(new URLPattern(p).exec('http://a/b/xyz')?.pathname.groups)\r\n```\r\nand a named parameter only logs one match?\r\n```js\r\np = 'http://a/b/:path*'\r\nconsole.log(new URLPattern(p).exec('http://a/b/')?.pathname.groups)\r\nconsole.log(new URLPattern(p).exec('http://a/b/xyz')?.pathname.groups)\r\n```\r\ni think there should be no differences between a named and unnamed wildcard... ",
